  "主要内容": "The July 2016 Manufacturing PMI® rose to 52.6, down 0.6 from June's 53.2, indicating continued growth in the manufacturing sector for the fifth month. New Orders grew slightly to 56.9, marking the seventh consecutive month of growth, with increases in Furniture & Related Products and Chemical Products, while Apparel, Leather & Allied Products saw a decline. Production increased by 0.7, while Employment and Inventories contracted. Prices rose, but at a slower pace. The Prices Index fell to 55%, reflecting a fifth consecutive month of rising raw material prices. Twenty-two percent of respondents reported paying higher prices, while 66% reported paying the same as in June. Supplier Deliveries slowed to 51.8%, down 3.6 percentage points from June. The report highlights that the manufacturing sector is growing slower, with some industries reporting increased demand for goods.",
